# r53_refuse_trace.patch — THE INSTRUMENT BEHIND §92 §3's MECHANISM CLAIM.
#
# 🚨 WHY THIS IS COMMITTED AS A PATCH RECIPE (rule 6, and r50's
# `item0j/r50_0j_trace.patch` precedent). §92 §3 says the measured site of the
# port's segment-solve declines under this fix is `fallback_gate ok=false` — the
# port-only fallback secant failing to converge — and NOT the `bad`/`inconsistent`
# condemnation path that round 52 and the round-53 plan both named. That claim
# was produced by a PROBE-ONLY trace that lived in /tmp and would have died with
# the session, leaving the round's most emphatic sentence unfalsifiable in both
# directions — the exact defect §92 diagnoses in round 52 one paragraph earlier.
# Found by r53's own adversarial audit, finding F4.
#
# APPLY WITH:  cd <copy of the tree> && patch -p1 < testplan/harness/r53refuse/r53_refuse_trace.patch
#
# ⚠️ RELATIVE a/ b/ HEADERS AND -p1, DELIBERATELY. The first version of this
# file carried ABSOLUTE paths (/root/pw/…, /tmp/pristine/…) in its diff headers.
# GNU patch ignores them and falls back to the relative name, but a tool that
# honours the absolute path would edit whatever tree that path names — from any
# copy. r53 audit pass 3. It also applied at offset +16 because it predated the
# loop caps; it is regenerated against the shipped tree and applies at offset 0.
# THEN:        DPTRACEREFUSE=1 go run ./cmd/goamort <screen...>   (trace -> stderr)
#
# 🚨 NEVER APPLY IT TO A TREE YOU INTEND TO SHIP. It writes to stderr from the
# engine; rule 7 says a driver's DEFAULT STDOUT is never disturbed, and this
# stays out of the shipped tree entirely rather than relying on that.
#
# EMITS, one line per return site of solveSegmentRate and its two callers' exits:
#   REFUSE ctr rate=<x> err=<e>        ComputeTrueRate raised errorflag (the lnn guard)
#   REFUSE site=cond_pre_fallback      condemned latch, before the fallback seed
#   REFUSE site=cond_post_fallback     condemned latch, after it
#   REFUSE site=fallback_gate ok=<b> r=<x>   the port-only fallback secant's gate
#   REFUSE site=prologue rem= bal= pay=      the rem<=0 / bal==0 / pay<=0 bail
--- a/internal/finance/amortization/dosport_walk.go
